## Bonus: promise cycle deadlock

Even without locks, you can create a never‑resolving graph:

```js
let resolveA, resolveB;
const a = new Promise((r) => { resolveA = r; });
const b = new Promise((r) => { resolveB = r; });

// resolveA only after b resolves; resolveB only after a resolves
resolveA(Promise.resolve().then(() => b));
resolveB(Promise.resolve().then(() => a));

// Neither ever settles:
a.then(() => console.log('a done')).catch(() => {});
```

This is the async analogue of a circular wait.

