Below are the most common edge cases when reading/writing files in JavaScript, split by **Node.js** (`fs`/`fs/promises`) and the **Browser File API**. Each includes a short explanation and idiomatic code.

---

## 1. Node.js (`fs/promises`)

### 1.1 File does not exist (ENOENT)
Always distinguish “not found” from other I/O errors; don’t crash on missing optional files.

```js
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';

async function readConfig(path) {
  try {
    return await readFile(path, 'utf8');
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 'ENOENT') return null;   // optional file
    throw err;                                 // real error
  }
}
```

### 1.2 Path is a directory (EISDIR)
Opening a directory for reading as a file throws `EISDIR`.

```js
import { readFile, stat } from 'node:fs/promises';

async function safeRead(path) {
  const s = await stat(path);   // throws ENOENT if missing
  if (s.isDirectory()) throw new Error('Expected a file, got a directory');
  return readFile(path, 'utf8');
}
```

### 1.3 Permission denied (EACCES / EPERM)
Common on protected paths or read-only mounts.

```js
try {
  await writeFile('/etc/hosts', 'x');
} catch (e) {
  if (e.code === 'EACCES' || e.code === 'EPERM') {
    console.error('No write permission');
  } else throw e;
}
```

### 1.4 Large files / memory exhaustion
`readFile` buffers the whole file. Use streams for anything big.

```js
import { createReadStream, createWriteStream } from 'node:fs';
import { pipeline } from 'node:stream/promises';

await pipeline(
  createReadStream('huge.log'),
  createWriteStream('copy.log')
);
```

### 1.5 Encoding & UTF-8 BOM
JSON/text files from Windows editors often start with `\uFEFF`.

```js
const raw = await readFile('data.json', 'utf8');
const text = raw.charCodeAt(0) === 0xFEFF ? raw.slice(1) : raw;
const data = JSON.parse(text);
```

### 1.6 Partial writes / crash safety (atomic writes)
`writeFile` truncates then writes; a crash mid-write leaves a corrupt file. Write to a temp file, then `rename` (atomic on same filesystem).

```js
import { writeFile, rename, unlink } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';

async function atomicWrite(target, content) {
  const tmp = join(tmpdir(), `${randomUUID()}.tmp`);
  await writeFile(tmp, content);
  await rename(tmp, target);   // atomic on POSIX; best-effort on Windows
}
```

### 1.7 Race conditions / concurrent access
Two processes writing the same file can interleave. Use exclusive create (`'wx'`) or file locks.

```js
import { open } from 'node:fs/promises';

// Fail if file already exists (atomic create)
const fh = await open('lock.pid', 'wx');
try {
  await fh.writeFile(String(process.pid));
  // ... work ...
} finally {
  await fh.close();
  await unlink('lock.pid'); // cleanup
}
```

For cross-process locking, use a library like `proper-lockfile` rather than hand-rolling.

### 1.8 Symlinks & path traversal
Resolving user input into a path can escape the intended directory.

```js
import { resolve, relative, isAbsolute } from 'node:path';

function safeJoin(base, untrusted) {
  const full = resolve(base, untrusted);
  const rel = relative(base, full);
  if (rel.startsWith('..') || isAbsolute(rel)) {
    throw new Error('Path traversal blocked');
  }
  return full;
}
```

Also beware `realpath` when following symlinks intentionally.

### 1.9 File descriptor leaks
Always close handles, even on errors. Use `try/finally` or (Node 22+) `using`.

```js
import { open } from 'node:fs/promises';

const fh = await open('data.bin');
try {
  const buf = await fh.readFile();
  // process
} finally {
  await fh.close();   // never skip
}
```

### 1.10 Empty files
`readFile` on an empty file returns `''` (text) or `Buffer(0)` (binary). Don’t treat empty as failure.

```js
const buf = await readFile('empty.bin'); // Buffer.byteLength === 0
```

### 1.11 Line endings (CRLF vs LF)
Normalise when parsing line-based data.

```js
const lines = (await readFile('log.txt', 'utf8'))
  .split(/\r?\n/)
  .filter(Boolean);
```

### 1.12 Watching files (debounce & ENOENT)
`fs.watch` can emit multiple events; files may be deleted between events.

```js
import { watch } from 'node:fs';

const w = watch('config.json', (event, filename) => {
  if (event === 'rename') return; // deleted/renamed; re-check existence
  // debounce heavy work
});
process.on('SIGINT', () => w.close());
```

### 1.13 JSON parse failures
File read can succeed but content be invalid.

```js
let data;
try {
  data = JSON.parse(await readFile('x.json', 'utf8'));
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof SyntaxError) data = {}; // fallback
  else throw e;
}
```

---

## 2. Browser File API

### 2.1 User cancels file picker
`showOpenFilePicker` rejects with `AbortError`; `<input>` may have empty `files`.

```js
// File System Access API
try {
  const [handle] = await window.showOpenFilePicker();
  const file = await handle.getFile();
  const text = await file.text();
} catch (e) {
  if (e.name === 'AbortError') return; // user cancelled
  throw e;
}
```

```html
<input type="file" id="f">
<script>
document.getElementById('f').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
  const file = e.target.files[0];
  if (!file) return; // cancelled / no selection
});
</script>
```

### 2.2 Reading very large files → memory blow-up
`File.text()` / `File.arrayBuffer()` load everything. Stream instead.

```js
const stream = file.stream();
const reader = stream.getReader();
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  // process chunk (Uint8Array)
}
```

### 2.3 Binary vs text confusion
Don’t assume text; sniff or respect user choice.

```js
// Safe: let FileReader decide per mode
const reader = new FileReader();
reader.onload = () => console.log(typeof reader.result);
reader.readAsText(file);   // string
// reader.readAsArrayBuffer(file); // ArrayBuffer
```

### 2.4 MIME type is unreliable
Browsers guess from extension; spoofed/mismatched types happen.

```js
// Validate by content, not file.type
const buf = await file.arrayBuffer();
const bytes = new Uint8Array(buf);
const isPng = bytes[0] === 0x89 && bytes[1] === 0x50;
```

### 2.5 File System Access API permission revocation
Permission can be revoked mid-session; re-request.

```js
const opts = { mode: 'readwrite' };
if (await handle.queryPermission(opts) !== 'granted') {
  if (await handle.requestPermission(opts) !== 'granted') throw new Error('Permission denied');
}
```

### 2.6 Writing files (Save As) can be cancelled
`showSaveFilePicker` also throws `AbortError`.

```js
let handle;
try {
  handle = await window.showSaveFilePicker({ suggestedName: 'out.txt' });
} catch (e) {
  if (e.name === 'AbortError') return;
  throw e;
}
const w = await handle.createWritable();
await w.write('hello');
await w.close(); // flush
```

### 2.7 Zero-byte / empty files
Handle gracefully; don’t assume content.

```js
if (file.size === 0) console.warn('Empty file selected');
```

### 2.8 Drag-and-drop: directories
`DataTransferItem` may be a directory; `getAsFile()` returns null.

```js
for (const item of e.dataTransfer.items) {
  const entry = item.webkitGetAsEntry?.();
  if (entry?.isDirectory) { /* recurse via FileSystemDirectoryReader */ continue; }
  const f = item.getAsFile();
  if (f) handleFile(f);
}
```

