### Key takeaways

| Concept | Syntax | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Declaration | `function f(a,b){}` | Hoisted; has own `this` |
| Expression | `const f = function(){}` | Not hoisted |
| Arrow | `const f = (a,b) => a+b` | Lexical `this`; no `arguments` |
| Default | `function f(a=1){}` | Evaluated at call time; can use earlier params |
| Rest | `function f(...args){}` | Real Array; must be last param |
| Spread | `f(...arr)` | Expands iterable into args |
| Destructure | `function f({a,b}){}` | Great for “named parameters” |
| Callback/HOF | `arr.map(x=>...)` | Functions are first-class values |
| Closure | Factory returns inner fn | Private state via scope |
| Async | `async function f(){ await ... }` | Returns a Promise |
| IIFE | `(() => {...})()` | Private scope, module pattern |
| Class method | `method(){}` / `field = () => {}` | Arrow field preserves `this` |

