## 3. Typical use cases

| Use case | Why static typing helps |
|---|---|
| **Large codebases / teams** | Shared contracts reduce miscommunication. |
| **Public libraries / SDKs** | `.d.ts` declaration files give consumers autocomplete and safety. |
| **React / Vue components** | Props typed via interfaces prevent invalid JSX. |
| **API clients** | Typed responses (e.g., `fetch<User>`) catch shape mismatches. |
| **Refactoring** | Rename a field → compiler flags every usage. |
| **Node backends** | Typed route handlers, DB models, env vars. |

