## Syntax

### 1. Creating strings

```js
const single = 'Hello';
const double = "World";
const backticks = `Hello ${double}`; // template literal

// Multiline
const multi = `Line 1
Line 2`;

// Escapes
const escaped = "He said \"hi\"\nand left\t...";
```

### 2. Template literals

Template literals allow interpolation and multiline text:

```js
const name = "Ada";
const score = 42;

const msg = `${name} scored ${score} points.`;
console.log(msg); // "Ada scored 42 points."
```

### 3. Tagged templates

A function can process template parts and interpolated values:

```js
function upper(strings, ...values) {
  return strings.reduce((acc, str, i) => {
    const value = values[i] ? String(values[i]).toUpperCase() : "";
    return acc + str + value;
  }, "");
}

const result = upper`Name: ${"ada"}, City: ${"paris"}`;
console.log(result); // "Name: ADA, City: PARIS"
```

