## Core String Operations

### Length and indexing

```js
const s = "hello";
console.log(s.length); // 5
console.log(s[0]);     // "h"
console.log(s.charAt(1)); // "e"
```

Note: missing index returns `undefined` with bracket access, but `charAt()` returns `""`.

```js
const emoji = "😀";
console.log(emoji.length); // 2 (surrogate pair)
console.log([...emoji].length); // 1 (code points)
```

### Concatenation

```js
const a = "Hello";
const b = "World";

console.log(a + " " + b);   // "Hello World"
console.log(a.concat(" ", b)); // "Hello World"
```

Template literals are usually clearer.

### Searching

```js
const text = "JavaScript is great";

console.log(text.includes("Script"));       // true
console.log(text.startsWith("Java"));        // true
console.log(text.endsWith("great"));         // true
console.log(text.indexOf("is"));            // 10
console.log(text.lastIndexOf("a"));         // 3
```

### Extracting substrings

```js
const s = "abcdef";

console.log(s.slice(1, 4));      // "bcd"
console.log(s.substring(1, 4));  // "bcd"
console.log(s.slice(-2));       // "ef" (negative supported by slice)
```

Prefer `slice()` in most cases because it supports negative indices.

### Transforming

```js
const s = "  Hello World  ";

console.log(s.trim());               // "Hello World"
console.log(s.trimStart());         // "Hello World  "
console.log(s.toLowerCase());        // "  hello world  "
console.log(s.toUpperCase());        // "  HELLO WORLD  "
console.log(s.replace("World", "JS")); // "  Hello JS  "
console.log(s.replaceAll("l", "L"));  // "  HeLLo WorLd  "
```

Important: `replace()` with a string replaces only the first match. Use regex with `g` or `replaceAll()` for all matches.

### Splitting and joining

```js
const csv = "a,b,c";
const parts = csv.split(",");
console.log(parts); // ["a", "b", "c"]

const joined = parts.join(" | ");
console.log(joined); // "a | b | c"
```

### Padding and repeating

```js
console.log("7".padStart(3, "0")); // "007"
console.log("ab".repeat(3));      // "ababab"
```

