## Performance Notes

- Strings are immutable, so repeated concatenation in tight loops can be inefficient.
- For building large strings, use an array and `join()`:

```js
const parts = [];
for (let i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
  parts.push(`item ${i}`);
}
const result = parts.join("\n");
```

- Regex compilation can be reused; avoid creating the same regex repeatedly in hot loops.
- `replaceAll` is often clearer than global regex replacement.

