## Common Pitfalls

```js
// 1. Strings are immutable
let s = "hello";
s.toUpperCase();
console.log(s); // "hello", not "HELLO"

// 2. length is UTF-16 code units
console.log("😀".length); // 2

// 3. replace replaces first match only (unless regex has g)
console.log("a-a".replace("-", "+")); // "a+a"? Actually "a+a"? first dash only: "a+a"? yes "a+a"? Wait "a-a".replace("-","+") => "a+a"? no, "a+a"? string "a-a": replace first '-' => "a+a"? Actually result "a+a"? yes.
```

