### Key takeaways

| Concept | Notes |
|---|---|
| `var` | Function-scoped, hoisted; legacy—avoid. |
| `let` | Block-scoped, reassignable. |
| `const` | Block-scoped, binding fixed; object/array *contents* still mutable. |
| Primitives | `string`, `number`, `boolean`, `null`, `undefined`, `symbol`, `bigint`. |
| References | `object`, `array`, `function`, plus built-ins (`Date`, `Map`, `Set`). |
| Type checking | `typeof` is unreliable for `null` (`"object"`) and arrays; use `Array.isArray` and explicit `=== null`. |
| Coercion | JS coerces freely with `+`, `-`, `==`, etc.; prefer explicit `Number()`, `String()`, `Boolean()` and `===`. |

