## Typical use cases

| Use case | Pattern |
|---|---|
| **CRUD** | `GET /resource`, `POST`, `PUT/PATCH`, `DELETE` with typed DTOs |
| **Pagination** | Query params typed as `Record<string, string \| number>` |
| **Auth** | Attach `Authorization: Bearer <token>` via interceptor |
| **File upload** | `FormData`, set `Content-Type` automatically |
| **Long polling / SSE** | `ReadableStream` or `EventSource` |
| **Cancellation** | `AbortController` + `signal` |
| **Retry/backoff** | Wrap fetch in a loop with exponential delay |

### Pagination example

```ts
interface Page<T> {
  items: T[];
  nextCursor?: string;
}

async function listUsers(cursor?: string): Promise<Page<User>> {
  const params = new URLSearchParams();
  if (cursor) params.set("cursor", cursor);
  const res = await fetch(`/api/users?${params}`);
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error("Failed");
  return res.json();
}
```

### Cancellation example

```ts
const controller = new AbortController();

fetch("/api/slow", { signal: controller.signal })
  .then((r) => r.json())
  .catch((e) => {
    if (e.name === "AbortError") console.log("Cancelled");
  });

// later
controller.abort();
```

### File upload example

```ts
async function upload(file: File) {
  const form = new FormData();
  form.append("file", file);
  const res = await fetch("/api/upload", { method: "POST", body: form });
  return res.json();
}
```

