## Common collection and conversion patterns

### Slice vs view

```ts
const original = new Uint8Array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]);

// subarray: view into same memory, no copy
const view = original.subarray(1, 4);

// slice: copy into new buffer
const copy = original.slice(1, 4);
```

### Concatenate bytes

```ts
function concat(...parts: Uint8Array[]): Uint8Array {
  const total = parts.reduce((n, p) => n + p.length, 0);
  const result = new Uint8Array(total);
  let offset = 0;

  for (const part of parts) {
    result.set(part, offset);
    offset += part.length;
  }

  return result;
}
```

### Convert `ArrayBuffer` ↔ typed array

```ts
const ab = new ArrayBuffer(4);
const u8 = new Uint8Array(ab);

// Detached transfer example in modern environments:
const transferred = ab.transfer(); // moves ownership; original becomes detached
const recipient = new Uint8Array(transferred);
```

