## 5. Signed vs unsigned & modulo wrapping

```ts
const u = new Uint8Array([255]);
const i = new Int8Array(u.buffer);

console.log(u[0]); // 255
console.log(i[0]); // -1

// Constructor coercion wraps
const w = new Uint8Array([256, -1]);
console.log(w);    // [0, 255]

// Bitwise ops are 32-bit signed
const x = 0xFFFFFFFF | 0;
console.log(x);    // -1  (not 4294967295)
```

**Edge case:** converting bytes to numbers via `|`, `<<`, etc. silently sign-extends; use `>>> 0` for unsigned.

