## 6. Text encoding: invalid UTF-8, BOM, lone surrogates

```ts
const dec = new TextDecoder("utf-8", { fatal: true });
try {
  dec.decode(new Uint8Array([0xFF]));
} catch (e) {
  console.error("invalid UTF-8");
}

// BOM handling
const withBom = new Uint8Array([0xEF, 0xBB, 0xBF, ...new TextEncoder().encode("hi")]);
const dec2 = new TextDecoder("utf-8", { ignoreBOM: false });
console.log(JSON.stringify(dec2.decode(withBom))); // "hi" (BOM stripped by default)

// Lone surrogate round-trip
const s = "\uD800";
const bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(s);   // replacement char bytes
const back = new TextDecoder().decode(bytes);
console.log(s === back); // false often
```

**Edge case:** `TextEncoder` only supports UTF-8; non-UTF-8 needs `TextDecoder` with label (e.g. `"utf-16le"`), and availability varies.

