## 10. Out-of-bounds reads/writes

```ts
const u = new Uint8Array(4);
console.log(u[10]);        // undefined (not 0, not throw)
u[10] = 5;                 // silently ignored in non-strict? actually no-op for out of range typed array index? 
// Typed arrays: out-of-range sets ignored, no throw.

const dv = new DataView(new ArrayBuffer(4));
// dv.getUint32(1);        // RangeError: Offset is outside bounds
```

**Edge case:** TypedArray out-of-range access is a no-op read (`undefined`) / ignored write; DataView throws. Inconsistent error behavior.

---

## 11. Streams: partial chunks & backpressure

```ts
async function readAll(stream: ReadableStream<Uint8Array>): Promise<Uint8Array> {
  const reader = stream.getReader();
  const chunks: Uint8Array[] = [];
  let total = 0;
  while (true) {
    const { value, done } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    chunks.push(value);
    total += value.byteLength;
  }
  const out = new Uint8Array(total);
  let off = 0;
  for (const c of chunks) { out.set(c, off); off += c.byteLength; }
  return out;
}
```

**Edge case:** a single `read()` may return a partial chunk; never assume one read = whole message. Also handle `value` possibly being a view with non-zero `byteOffset`.

