## 12. `byteOffset` / views into larger buffers

```ts
const big = new Uint8Array(100);
const view = big.subarray(10, 20);     // byteOffset=10, byteLength=10
const u32 = new Uint32Array(view.buffer, view.byteOffset, view.byteLength / 4);
// must pass byteOffset! Otherwise reads from start of big buffer.
```

**Edge case:** creating a TypedArray from `view.buffer` without `byteOffset` ignores the view's window.

