## 4. Style principles demonstrated

| Principle | Where it shows |
|---|---|
| **Strict types** | `tsconfig strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` |
| **Immutability** | `readonly` fields, `[...this.users]` copies, `readonly IUser[]` |
| **Single source of truth** | Zod schema drives validation + inferred type |
| **Naming conventions** | `IUser` interface, `CreateUserInput` type, `ROLES` constant, `camelCase` methods |
| **Encapsulation** | private `users` array, only public methods |
| **No magic strings** | `ROLES.ADMIN` instead of `"admin"` |
| **Explicit returns** | `findById(id): IUser \| undefined` |
| **No null ambiguity** | `undefined` for missing (not `null`) |
| **Imports** | `import type` for type-only, `.js` extension for ESM |
| **Errors** | Throw typed `Error` with context; `safeParse` instead of throwing on parse |
| **No mutation surprises** | `update` preserves `id`/`createdAt` explicitly |

